{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "Typed system-function calls under MIR-Direct. Tune6 L3 landed native math lowering: math.* transcendentals with statically-numeric scalar arguments now import the libm symbol (sin, sqrt) and call it with a d->d prototype instead of the boxed fn_math_* wrapper. Deliberate update -- before L3 this fixture expected 'import fn_math_sin' / 'import fn_math_sqrt'. The unboxed fn_*_u / fn_abs_i specializations remain C-transpiler-only and stay forbidden. fn_abs stays boxed on purpose: abs/round/floor/ceil/trunc/min/max are type preserving (abs(-5) is int 5), so lowering them to a double-returning native call would change the result type. fn_pow here is the ** operator, not math.pow.",
  "checks": [
    {
      "in_func": "*",
      "expect": [
        "import\tfn_pow",
        "import\tfn_abs",
        "import\tsin",
        "import\tsqrt"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        "import\tfn_math_sin",
        "import\tfn_math_sqrt",
        "import\tfn_pow_u",
        "import\tfn_abs_i",
        "import\tfn_min2_u",
        "import\tfn_max2_u",
        "import\tfn_sign_i",
        "import\tfn_sign_f"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
